# Google Cloud project for Vertex AI (Gemini Flash Lite classification pass).
GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT=your-gcp-project
VERTEX_AI_REGION_GEMINI=global

# Credentials for Vertex. The daemon is a long-running unattended service, so it uses a
# long-lived service-account key rather than developer ADC (which expires and needs a
# browser reauth, wedging the daemon — see docs/design/durable-vertex-auth.md). google-auth
# honors this env var with no code change.
# The SA may live in a DIFFERENT project than GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT: many orgs enforce
# constraints/iam.disableServiceAccountKeyCreation on the project that runs inference, so
# mint the key in a project that allows keys and grant that SA roles/aiplatform.user on the
# inference project. Mint with:
#   gcloud iam service-accounts keys create ~/.config/tmux-rc/vertex-sa.json \
#     --iam-account=tmux-rc-classifier@YOUR-KEY-PROJECT.iam.gserviceaccount.com
#   chmod 600 ~/.config/tmux-rc/vertex-sa.json
# Use an absolute path (google-auth does not expand ~).
GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/home/YOU/.config/tmux-rc/vertex-sa.json

# Restrict watching to a single pane (default: watch every pane on the server).
# Always works: a pane id ("%3") or a numeric tmux address ("work:0" / "work:0.0" —
# the window/pane INDEX, not the window name).
# Also accepted: the pane's derived label — the window name if you named the window,
# else the session name, else the cwd basename ("label" / "label.N"). So on a named
# window the SESSION name does not match; only the window name does.
# NOTE: the title on a card in the UI is often NOT a valid target — it may be the
# agent's own pane title or an LLM-refined name. Pane ids always work.
# TMUXRC_TARGET=work:0.0

# HTTP bind. Localhost, because the API is unauthenticated and /send injects keystrokes
# into your terminals — reaching it from the LAN must be a deliberate choice. Uncomment
# the 0.0.0.0 line to browse from a phone on the same (trusted) network; off-LAN access
# should go through a tunnel that authenticates, not a wider bind.
TMUXRC_HOST=127.0.0.1
#TMUXRC_HOST=0.0.0.0
# 18030, not 8080: every dev box already has something on 8080. 1803X spells R,C.
TMUXRC_PORT=18030

# Docs site served at /docs. Point at the Hugo build output (`make docs`, built with
# --baseURL /docs/). Unset = default docs-site/serve next to the package; leave the dir
# absent to not serve docs (dev uses `make docs-dev`, Hugo's own hot-reload server). Use
# an absolute path when running the daemon from outside the checkout.
# TMUXRC_DOCS_DIR=/absolute/path/to/tmux-rc/docs-site/serve

# Benchmark telemetry (optional). Unset endpoint = telemetry disabled (daemon runs
# normally offline). Points at any OTLP/gRPC receiver, which is expected to flatten the
# records to object storage. Bearer token goes in OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS.
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4319
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS=authorization=Bearer <token>
# TMUXRC_QSDEBUG=1   # also send raw pane text + model output JSON (privacy: contents → sink)

# Live Mode (voice) — talk to your whole session. Uses Vertex like the classifier but
# needs a Live-capable model on a region that serves it (NOT flash-lite / "global").
# OFF by default (the voice UX is still being tuned); set to 1 to show the mic button
# and allow /api/live-mode. The dim/placeholder markers and window naming it rides in
# with are always on — they help the phone cards regardless of this flag.
# TMUXRC_LIVE_MODE=1
# TMUXRC_LIVE_REGION=us-central1
#
# Which voice models the Live button offers: a JSON list inline, or a path to a file
# holding one (the TMUXRC_LAUNCHERS shape). Unset = Gemini 2.5 on Vertex, no picker.
# With two or more OFFERED entries the Live button opens a picker; an entry whose keys
# are missing stays configured but off the menu until they appear — no config edit.
# Per entry: label (what the picker shows — the ONLY thing the browser ever sends back),
# model (the provider's model id; for Azure the DEPLOYMENT name, by convention the same
# string), backend (vertex | gemini-api | openai | azure-openai), rates (USD per 1M
# tokens: text_in, text_out, audio_in, audio_out, text_cached, audio_cached — a missing
# rate takes Gemini 2.5's, so a new model's cost is never a silent zero; a missing
# CACHED rate takes the entry's own uncached one, so no published discount means no
# discount), and backend flags: proactive_audio (Gemini on Vertex; 3.1 Flash Live
# rejects it), voice (OpenAI voice, default marin). The cached rates matter on OpenAI:
# Realtime re-bills the whole context every response, most of it cached at ~1-3% of list.
# Rates below are the Sep 2026 list prices — check the provider's price page.
# TMUXRC_LIVE_MODELS='[
#   {"label": "Gemini 2.5", "model": "gemini-live-2.5-flash-native-audio", "proactive_audio": true},
#   {"label": "Gemini 3.1", "model": "gemini-3.1-flash-live-preview", "backend": "gemini-api"},
#   {"label": "GPT 2.1", "model": "gpt-realtime-2.1", "backend": "openai",
#    "rates": {"text_in": 4, "text_out": 24, "audio_in": 32, "audio_out": 64,
#              "text_cached": 0.4, "audio_cached": 0.4}},
#   {"label": "GPT 2.1 mini", "model": "gpt-realtime-2.1-mini", "backend": "openai",
#    "rates": {"text_in": 0.6, "text_out": 2.4, "audio_in": 10, "audio_out": 20,
#              "text_cached": 0.06, "audio_cached": 0.3}},
#   {"label": "GPT 2.1 (Azure)", "model": "gpt-realtime-2.1", "backend": "azure-openai",
#    "rates": {"text_in": 4, "text_out": 24, "audio_in": 32, "audio_out": 64,
#              "text_cached": 0.4, "audio_cached": 0.4}}
# ]'
# The keys those backends need do NOT go in this file. Put them in
# ~/.config/tmux-rc/openai.env (chmod 600) — GEMINI_API_KEY, OPENAI_API_KEY,
# AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY + AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT (the resource host: *.openai.azure.com or
# *.cognitiveservices.azure.com). The daemon and research/live-eval read that file; it
# lives outside every checkout so no worktree .env or commit can carry a key.

# The daemon prefers IPv4 for outbound connections (an advertised-but-dead IPv6 route
# otherwise starves streaming handshakes). Set to 0 if your v6 works and your v4 doesn't.
# TMUXRC_PREFER_IPV4=1
